The patch implements most of the stuff discussed here:
(http://groups.google.com/group/rec.games.roguelike.nethack/browse_thread/thread/8bb7dea261c0fab5/f94ef11f29ca5fe1)

It also adds one new bigroom, and one new minetown. Comments on these
designs are welcome!

A FEW NOTES:
* Shallow water is referred to as PUDDLE terrain within the code.
Strange, that.
* I decided that shallow water shouldn't drown tiny monsters, because
the "underwater" code seems to be dependant upon all water glyphs being
'}' and I didn't feel like taking that apart.
* So, you can't drown in shallow water at all.
* Shallow water can't be dug into. (For what it's worth, neither can
deep water.)
* Boulders dropped in pools or moats still create floor. I'm assuming
that boulders are tall enough to stick out of the water even when they
touch bottom. (IDEA: huge monsters shouldn't be able to drown in pools
or moats.)
* Digging next to shallow water doesn't create a pool.

ATTENTION:
In making this patch I had to alter about a dozen special cases related
to pool terrain such that shallow water was included as well. (I didn't
tweak is_pool() because it refers to "drownable" terrain.) I _think_ I
got them all but it's possible that I missed a few. Feedback will be
appreciated!



